  "_about": "a peregrine falcon on the hunt: long, pointed, narrow wings swept back from the wrist, the stiff unslotted primaries, a longish narrow tail barred dark; slate-blue above, the black hood and the black moustache down the white cheek, below white barred dark; a short hooked bill on the yellow cere, the yellow eye-ring, yellow feet drawn up (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
